# Frozen projection receipt: the disclosed scene as navigable semantics,
# driven end to end. The pane freezes exactly what the graphshell endpoint
# serves a remote peer, and `assert a11y` reads the same AccessKit tree
# graphshell_client::frozen builds for any host — so this is the projection
# grammar plan's B1 verification loop closing on a real app: probe-driven,
# no synthetic OS input, semantic tree asserted by role and name.
# Offline by design: mere:// nodes only. FRESH profile.
settle 30
key escape

# Two named nodes for the projection to read.
open mere://harbor-notes
wait
open mere://beacon-notes
wait
assert nodes >= 2

# Summon the pane; the palette row comes from the pane registry.
act Open Frozen Projection pane
settle 40
capture 01_frozen_projection_open

# The document announces itself, and every instance is reachable by name in
# the stitched application tree. Labels come from node_display_label, the
# same label the endpoint's presentation plane sends.
assert a11y document: Disclosed projection
assert a11y harbor-notes
assert a11y beacon-notes

# The instances group states its own count-bearing label, so a reader knows
# the size of what they are about to walk.
assert a11y list:

capture 02_frozen_projection_asserted
